          {
            "title": "Multiple values",
            "id": 88373,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Tuples are useful because they allow us to return multiple values from a function, like the highest and lowest scores from a list.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"get_scores_data\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(scores_list)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  highest_score = max(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  lowest_score = min(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" highest_score, lowest_score\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"105\" endIndex=\"111\" /><option startIndex=\"112\" endIndex=\"139\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return</code>, followed by <code>highest_score, lowest_score</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A function can return several values as a tuple. Separate them with a comma.</p><p>Return <code>highest_score</code> first, then <code>lowest_score</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"get_scores_data\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"scores_list\" /><text value=\")\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"highest_score\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"max\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"scores_list\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"lowest_score\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"min\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"scores_list\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"highest_score\" /><text value=\",\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"lowest_score\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"105\" endIndex=\"111\" /><option startIndex=\"112\" endIndex=\"139\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"print\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"lowest_score, highest_score\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return</code>, followed by <code>highest_score, lowest_score</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Return a tuple",
            "id": 88377,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To return a tuple, we code the values that we wish to return separated by a comma <code>,</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"get_scores_data\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(scores_list)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  highest_score = max(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  lowest_score = min(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" highest_score, lowest_score\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"125\" endIndex=\"126\" /></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>,</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "No parentheses",
            "id": 88378,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Even though we're returning a tuple, parentheses are not necessary.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"get_scores_data\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(scores_list)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  highest_score = max(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  lowest_score = min(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" highest_score, lowest_score\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"105\" endIndex=\"111\" /><option startIndex=\"112\" endIndex=\"139\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"def\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return</code>, followed by <code>highest_score, lowest_score</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When we return several values, we separate them with a comma and no parentheses are needed.</p><p>Return <code>highest_score</code> first, then <code>lowest_score</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"get_scores_data\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(scores_list)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  highest_score = max(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  lowest_score = min(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" highest_score, lowest_score\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"105\" endIndex=\"111\" /><option startIndex=\"112\" endIndex=\"125\" /><option startIndex=\"125\" endIndex=\"126\" /><option startIndex=\"127\" endIndex=\"139\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"scores_list\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"print\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return</code>, followed by <code>highest_score</code>, <code>,</code>, and finally <code>lowest_score</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Store return value",
            "id": 88379,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To store a tuple returned by a function, we assign the function call's result to a variable like <code>data</code>, as usual.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"get_scores_data\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(scores_list)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  highest_score = max(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  lowest_score = min(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" highest_score, lowest_score\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"31\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"data = get_scores_data(scores)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(data)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"162\" endIndex=\"166\" /><option startIndex=\"167\" endIndex=\"168\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\",\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"(80, 17)\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>data</code>, followed by <code>=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To store a returned tuple, assign the function call's result to a variable.</p><p>Store the tuple in <code>data</code> so the code prints <code>(80, 17)</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"get_scores_data\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(scores_list)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  highest_score = max(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  lowest_score = min(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" highest_score, lowest_score\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"31\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"data = get_scores_data(scores)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(data)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"162\" endIndex=\"166\" /><option startIndex=\"167\" endIndex=\"168\" /><option startIndex=\"169\" endIndex=\"184\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"scores\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"min\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"(80, 17)\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>data</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>get_scores_data</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Retrieve individual values",
            "id": 88380,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can then retrieve the individual values by their indices, like the highest score with <code>data[0]</code>, and the smallest with <code>data[1]</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"get_scores_data\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(scores_list)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  highest_score = max(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  lowest_score = min(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" highest_score, lowest_score\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"31\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"data = get_scores_data(scores)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"highest = data[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"smallest = data[\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;smallest score: \" /><text value=\"{smallest}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;highest score: \" /><text value=\"{highest}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"193\" endIndex=\"200\" /><option startIndex=\"222\" endIndex=\"229\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"return\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"smallest score: 17\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"highest score: 80\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>highest</code>, followed by <code>data[1]</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The lowest score sits at index <code>1</code> of the returned tuple. Store it in <code>smallest</code> so the code prints <code>smallest score: 17</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"get_scores_data\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(scores_list)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  highest_score = max(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  lowest_score = min(scores_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" highest_score, lowest_score\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"31\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"data = get_scores_data(scores)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"highest = data[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"smallest = data[\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;smallest score: \" /><text value=\"{smallest}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;highest score: \" /><text value=\"{highest}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"211\" endIndex=\"219\" /><option startIndex=\"222\" endIndex=\"229\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"data[0]\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"smallest score: 17\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"highest score: 80\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>smallest</code>, followed by <code>data[1]</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "When to return a tuple",
            "id": 88381,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Since tuples are immutable, we return a tuple when we won't need to modify it, but just use the values, like with a game's winners.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"get_top_three\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(players)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" players[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"], players[\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"], players[\" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"players = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Sue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Ed&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Ann&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Ty&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"top_three = get_top_three(players)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;First: \" /><text value=\"{top_three[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]}\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Second: \" /><text value=\"{top_three[\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]}\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Third: \" /><text value=\"{top_three[\" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]}\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"30\" endIndex=\"36\" /><option startIndex=\"37\" endIndex=\"71\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"First: Sue\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Second: Ed\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Third: Ann\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return</code>, followed by <code>players[0], players[1], players[2]</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Since tuples are immutable, return a tuple when you only need to use its values, not modify them.</p><p>Return the first three players in order so the code prints <code>First: Sue</code>, then Ed, then Ann.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"get_top_three\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(players)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" players[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"], players[\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"], players[\" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"players = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Sue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Ed&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Ann&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Ty&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"top_three = get_top_three(players)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;First: \" /><text value=\"{top_three[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]}\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Second: \" /><text value=\"{top_three[\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]}\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Third: \" /><text value=\"{top_three[\" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]}\" /><text value=\"&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"30\" endIndex=\"36\" /><option startIndex=\"37\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"players[1], players[0], players[2]\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"First: Sue\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Second: Ed\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Third: Ann\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return</code>, followed by <code>players[0], players[1], players[2]</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "When to return a list",
            "id": 88382,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When we want to be able to modify the returned collection of values, like updating a team member, we <code>return</code> a list like <code>team</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"form_team\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(players)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  team = []\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  team.append(players[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  team.append(players[\" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" team\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"players = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Sue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Ed&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Ann&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Ty&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"team = form_team(players)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"team[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"] = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Chloe&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(team)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"90\" endIndex=\"101\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"['Chloe', 'Ann']\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>return team</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Multiple values",
            "id": 88670,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What is one of the main uses of tuples?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Returning multiple values inside functions</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Displaying values</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Returning multiple values inside functions.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>One main use of tuples is returning multiple values from a function.</p><p>A function calculates both <code>width</code> and <code>height</code>. Which statement returns both results together?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>return width, height</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>print(width, height)</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>return width</code> followed by <code>return height</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return width, height</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Return a tuple",
            "id": 88671,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How do we separate the different values when returning multiple values from a function?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Using commas <code>,</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Using semicolons <code>;</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Using commas <code>,</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We separate multiple returned values with commas.</p><p>Which line correctly returns <code>lowest</code> and <code>highest</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>return lowest, highest</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>return lowest; highest</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>return lowest highest</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return lowest, highest</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: No parentheses",
            "id": 88672,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Do we need parentheses when returning multiple values?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">No, just the <code>return</code> keyword followed by the values</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Yes, around each individual value</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">No, just the <code>return</code> keyword followed by the values.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We do not need parentheses when returning multiple values, only <code>return</code> followed by the values.</p><p>What does <code>return name, age</code> send back to the caller?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A tuple containing <code>name</code> and <code>age</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Only <code>name</code>, because <code>age</code> is outside parentheses</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">An error, because each value needs its own parentheses</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A tuple containing <code>name</code> and <code>age</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Store return value",
            "id": 88673,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How can we save a tuple returned by a function?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">By storing it in a variable, like any other value</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">We can't save tuples returned by functions</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">By storing it in a variable, like any other value.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We save a tuple returned by a function by storing it in a variable, like any other value.</p><p>Which line stores the tuple from <code>get_bounds()</code> in <code>bounds</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>bounds = get_bounds()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>bounds == get_bounds()</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>get_bounds(bounds)</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>bounds = get_bounds()</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Retrieve individual values",
            "id": 88674,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How do we retrieve the individual values from the tuple returned by a function?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">By their index</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">By their value</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">By their index.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We retrieve individual values from a returned tuple by their index.</p><p>The variable <code>profile</code> stores <code>(\"Mia\", 21)</code>. Which expression retrieves the age?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>profile[1]</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>profile[21]</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>profile.age</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>profile[1]</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: When to return a tuple",
            "id": 88675,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When should we return a tuple?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">When we're only interested in the individual values or don't intend to modify the tuple</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">When we intend to replace values in the tuple</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">When we're only interested in the individual values or don't intend to modify the tuple.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We should return a tuple when we need individual values and do not intend to modify them.</p><p>A function returns a location's fixed <code>latitude</code> and <code>longitude</code>. Which return value fits best?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A tuple containing the two coordinates</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A list intended for replacing either coordinate later</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">One string that joins both coordinates and hides the individual values</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A tuple containing the two coordinates.</p></body></html>"
