            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When should we return a list instead of a tuple?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">When we're interested in the values as a collection, and intend to modify the list</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">When the returned collection of values shouldn't be changed</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">When we're interested in the values as a collection, and intend to modify the list.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We should return a list when we need the values as a collection and intend to modify it.</p><p>A function returns shopping-cart items that users can add and remove later. Which return value fits best?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A list containing the cart items</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A tuple that should remain unchanged</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Only the first cart item instead of the collection</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A list containing the cart items.</p></body></html>",
